    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate is headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (81.25) and **Christian Yelich** (74.32), who provide our highest ceilings thanks to favorable matchups against Fedde and Ober, respectively. Both players benefit from \"slow delivery\" pitchers who are vulnerable to our elite stolen base strategy, allowing them to capitalize on the scarcest category in our 5x5 format. While **Yordan Alvarez** and **Kyle Schwarber** face a daunting matchup against Skenes, their elite xwOBA profiles keep them in the starting lineup despite the high SP_xERA of the opposition. Meanwhile, **Hyeseong Kim** and **Carson Benge** are high-value starts today; both face extremely favorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs north of 6.00, essentially acting as \"must-starts\" to maximize our daily efficiency scores.\n\nThe decision to keep **Chase Meidroth** on the bench remains the most difficult roster choice today. With a score of 49.85, **Chase Meidroth** was arguably our most viable reserve, but he ultimately yielded to the superior platoon and order advantages possessed by **Luke Raley** and **Colt Keith**. We are effectively sacrificing depth to ensure we capitalize on the high-probability production of our primary starters. Investors should be aware of the \"Elite Catcher\" risk regarding **Trea Turner**, whose efficiency is hampered by the threat of Skenes\u2019s elite arm, and continue to monitor the status of **Caleb Durbin**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, and **Zac Veen**, who remain inactive or sidelined in the minors. We are operating with a clear focus on stolen base efficiency today, and provided weather holds, our current configuration optimizes our 5x5 standing against the league leaders.",
